# Lemon Herb Tofu Bowls

Based on [School Night Vegan - Easy Tofu Marinades](https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260112215657/https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Lemon Herb Tofu

- [ ] 2 (14-ounce) blocks [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cut into 1-inch cubes
- [ ] 1/4 cup [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] [Zest of 2 lemons]{ ing="lemon-zest" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup fresh [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } (about 2 lemons)
- [ ] 1 tablespoon fresh [thyme leaves]{ ing="thyme-leaves" } (or 1 teaspoon dried)
- [ ] 1 tablespoon fresh [rosemary]{ ing="rosemary" }, finely chopped (or 1 teaspoon dried)
- [ ] 2 tablespoons fresh [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 teaspoon [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 1 teaspoon [sea salt]{ ing="sea-salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 teaspoon [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [water]{ ing="water" }

### Bowl Components

- [ ] 1.5 cups [quinoa or farro]{ ing="quinoa-or-farro" } (uncooked)
- [ ] 3 cups [water or vegetable broth]{ ing="water-or-vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] 1 pint [cherry tomatoes]{ ing="cherry-tomatoes" }, halved
- [ ] 1 medium [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, diced
- [ ] 1 [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, diced
- [ ] 1 small [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] [Salt and black pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 4 cups [mixed greens]{ ing="mixed-greens" } (arugula, spinach, or spring mix)
- [ ] 1 cup [kalamata olives]{ ing="kalamata-olives" }, pitted and halved
- [ ] 1 cup [canned chickpeas]{ ing="canned-chickpeas" }, drained and rinsed
- [ ] 1/2 cup [crumbled feta cheese]{ ing="crumbled-feta-cheese" } (omit for vegan)

### Tahini Lemon Dressing

- [ ] 1/4 cup [tahini]{ ing="tahini" }
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 clove [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2-4 tablespoons [water]{ ing="water" } to thin
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

## Recipe

### Marinate the Tofu

1. Press [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } for at least 30 minutes to remove excess moisture, then cut into 1-inch cubes
1. In a bowl or ziplock bag, whisk together [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [lemon]{ ing="lemon-zest" } zest, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, thyme, [rosemary]{ ing="rosemary" }, [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [salt]{ ing="sea-salt" }, [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, and [water]{ ing="water" }
1. Add [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes and toss to coat. Refrigerate for minimum 30 minutes or up to overnight

### Cook the Grains

1. Rinse [quinoa or farro]{ ing="quinoa-or-farro" } under cold [water]{ ing="water" }
1. Combine grains and [water]{ ing="water" }/[broth]{ ing="water-or-vegetable-broth" } in a pot. Bring to a boil
1. For quinoa: Reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer 15 minutes. Let sit covered 5 minutes, then fluff
1. For [farro]{ ing="quinoa-or-farro" }: Reduce heat to medium-low, cover, and simmer 25-30 minutes until tender. Drain excess liquid if needed

### Roast the Tofu and Vegetables

1. Heat oven to 425°F and line two baking sheets with parchment paper
1. Remove [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } from marinade (reserve marinade) and spread on one baking sheet in a single layer
1. On second baking sheet, toss [cherry tomatoes]{ ing="cherry-tomatoes" }, [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, [bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, and [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" } with [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, [salt]{ ing="sea-salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
1. Roast both sheets for 20-25 minutes, flipping [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } halfway through and tossing vegetables once, until tofu is golden and vegetables are caramelized

### Make Tahini Dressing

1. In a small bowl, whisk together [tahini]{ ing="tahini" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
1. Add [water]{ ing="water" } 1 tablespoon at a time until dressing reaches pourable consistency
1. Season with [salt]{ ing="sea-salt" } to taste

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide [quinoa or farro]{ ing="quinoa-or-farro" } among bowls
1. Top with [mixed greens]{ ing="mixed-greens" }, roasted [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, roasted vegetables, [chickpeas]{ ing="canned-chickpeas" }, and [olives]{ ing="kalamata-olives" }
1. Sprinkle with feta if using
1. Drizzle with [tahini]{ ing="tahini" } [lemon]{ ing="lemon-zest" } dressing and any reserved [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } marinade

## Notes

- **Meal prep advantage**: All components can be prepared in advance and stored separately for 4-5 days. Assemble bowls fresh with greens and dressing
- **Tahini substitute**: Equal amount sunflower seed butter, almond butter, or cashew butter. For dressing only, Greek yogurt works
- **Grain alternatives**: Use brown rice, couscous, or bulgur wheat instead of quinoa/farro
- **Herb substitutes**: If fresh herbs unavailable, use all dried (1 tsp each thyme, rosemary, oregano; 2 tsp dried parsley). Let marinade sit longer for flavors to develop
- **Protein boost**: Add hard-boiled eggs or white beans for additional protein
- **Make it Greek**: Add cucumber, use orzo instead of quinoa, and serve with tzatziki instead of tahini dressing
- **Summer variation**: Grill marinated tofu and vegetables instead of roasting for smoky flavor
